{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1211896-is-morality-done-backwards","id":1211896,"title":"Is morality done backwards?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-26T11:01:59-07:00","id":1211896,"title":"Is morality done backwards?","content":"Thought this a while.<br /> <br /> Is morality done backwards?<br /> <br /> Getting 5 dice for a Humanity 10 violation, means a vampire is more likely to get an exceptional success on an EXTREMELY obscure point of morality, not murder or torture.<br /> <br /> Which I have an easier time imagining producing an epipheny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T11:33:55-07:00","id":1211910,"title":"","content":"You can still get an exceptional success even on just 3 dice but yes, the system is conceptualized so those -are- exceptional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T11:39:11-07:00","id":1211913,"title":"","content":"I know but it being more likely with laughably petty indiscretions like &quot;Witnessing a supernatural act the first time&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T11:47:42-07:00","id":1211914,"title":"","content":"First off, it's Integrity now, Integrity is the polestar the other stats deviate away from and mirror now.<br /> <br /> Second off, why <i>shouldn't</i> minor, pettier violations of Integrity-alikes be easier to succeed at? Why <i>shouldn't </i>devouring my best friend cause more harm to/be harder to reconcile with my sense of Integrity or Humanity than just watching someone conjure coins out of nowhere?<br /> <br /> This question makes no sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T12:22:55-07:00","id":1211930,"title":"","content":"I'm on lunch, so let's break this down a bit.<br /> <br /> First, as Arc said, Integrity and Morality and not the same. Further more, Humanity is not the same as either, although mechanically it is more informed by Integrity than Morality.<br /> <br /> Secondly, it is important to understand that the violations are not alone in this matter, it is important to take the Humanity score itself into account as well. When your Humanity is very high you are extremely tied to the concept of humanity as a central pillar of your sense of self. When you commit a sin that is high on the list then you are shaking that very pristine version of yourself in your head. If you fail then you realize that you aren't as human as you thought and it breaks you a bit. If you succeed then you remain blissfully unaware of how you are losing your Humanity. If you get an Exceptional Success then you are managing to not only retain the facade but actually reinforce it. This makes sense sense it is easier to reinforce while you are still very sure of it (but also the simplest things are triggers because it is such a false state).<br /> <br /> When you are committing a far more grievous sin like murder, you are likely to be shaken far more and have a much harder time having a positive reinforcing effect from the act. If you have low Humanity then it is even worse because you no longer even hold the delusion that you retain your Humanity so why would committing a heinous act ever reinforce that image except in the most extreme lucky circumstances.<br /> <br /> As a third point, Exceptional Success on a Humanity roll are not the only epiphanies that arise from testing your Humanity, they are just the ones that reinforce the human self image. It is also an epiphany to realize just how monstrous you have become and forsake the idea of ever going back.<br /> <br /> Similar, but different, logic follows for Integrity and the other 2e equivalents based on what those stats are trying to emulate.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1211896-is-morality-done-backwards?p=1211913#post1211913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know but it being more likely with laughably petty indiscretions like &quot;Witnessing a supernatural act the first time&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't see this.<br /> <br /> So to talk more about Integrity specifically. It is a stated part of the setting that the human psyche has a tendency to ignore or rationalize away the supernatural. Given that, this particular example makes sense since an Exceptional Success shows that the character not only ignored the supernatural ( and thus maintains their world view, also known as Integrity) but the rationalization is used as a mental model to convince themselves that they understand the world BETTER now and thus reinforces their Integrity.<br /> <br /> The lower Breaking Points represent things that would shake your world view more and are harder to rationalize away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":". 04-26-2018, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:21:49-07:00","id":1211981,"title":"","content":"the thing was an exceptional success Gives a beneficial condition but is easier for me to imagine with something major.<br /> <br /> Only way I can imagine it with something Minor is a kindred with humanity walking for most of the day in the sun and going &quot;It hurt Guess thats what separates me from mortals now&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:48:02-07:00","id":1211997,"title":"","content":"First of all, the way Exceptionals work doesn't mean Integrity or Humanity is done backwards. The core of Integrity/Humanity is that it's harder to achieve a success when exposed to something more traumatising/dehumanising, which is completely realistic (as far as vampires and the supernatural are realistic) and works as intended. That Exceptional Success is more common with more trivial breaking points is a side effect of the underlying dice system.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately there's no real good way of changing how it works mechanically.<br /> The first alternative would be to make more horrible breaking points easier to succeed at, which just doesn't make any sense.<br /> The second alternative would be to introduce a new mechanic to replace the Exceptional Success. Perhaps by changing the Exceptional threshold depending on the level of the breaking point, or introducing a second roll that is somehow inverted to the first roll. I would not recommend either because from a game design point of view they just add clutter to an otherwise pretty streamlined system.<br /> But what you can do without messing with the dice system is to narratively redefine what an Exceptional Success is. Rather than an epiphany that should arise from more dramatic moments, an Exceptional Success could instead mean that the character takes the breaking point in stride, without even being shaken by what they just experienced. I think that works perfectly because that would be more common with more trivial breaking points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T15:45:48-07:00","id":1212025,"title":"","content":"Another thing?<br /> <br /> If you're interested, we can discuss how to make revelations from &quot;minor&quot; incidents something easier to grok instead. Religion, philosophy, and science are actually full of amazing realizations born from incredibly small seemingly meaningless things. There are multiple philosophic approaches that argue revelation from &quot;small&quot; things are the more valuable ones because, essentially, they're the less obvious lessons. &quot;Punching someone causes them pain, and I feel bad because I have empathy,&quot; is a very surface level revelation. Most people learn this as young children. Sitting in a bathtub and realizing how the displacement of water relates to the mass of objects is the Eurkea moment after all, and is something insanely mundane.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T12:53:48-07:00","id":1212762,"title":"","content":"Ok lets say Harmony going a week in the same form (Never played forsaken nor do I wish to)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> or not hunting your own food?<br /> <br /> How to make an exceptional success there meaningful?<br /> <br /> <br /> on humanity... <br /> Can see now on lieing to defend the masquerade because your keeping humanity from unleashing a blood bath upon itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T15:30:57-07:00","id":1212816,"title":"","content":"Harmony probably isn't a good thing to bring into this, as Harmony works considerably differently than most Integrity equivalents. The ideal value if 5, and there's two sets of situations to roll for depending which direction from 5 it would take you. There's also no default Exceptional success or Dramatic Failure option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T17:28:21-07:00","id":1212849,"title":"","content":"ok<br /> <br /> Mage If he gets an exceptional success for &quot;Boiling tea leaves with magic&quot; How might he feel then? Like a fool? would he be able to drink the tea?<br /> <br /> A vampire performing a superhuman feat of prowless?<br /> <br /> or lying in direct defense of the masquerade?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 04-28-2018, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T18:32:20-07:00","id":1212872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1211896-is-morality-done-backwards?p=1212849#post1212849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok<br /> <br /> Mage If he gets an exceptional success for &amp;quot;Boiling tea leaves with magic&amp;quot; How might he feel then? Like a fool? would he be able to drink the tea?<br /> <br /> A vampire performing a superhuman feat of prowless?<br /> <br /> or lying in direct defense of the masquerade?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Wisdom is intresting, because it\u2019s more about being aware of yourself than being secure in your beliefs. So yeah, it would be you would feel like a fool. You would have the epithany of \u201cwhat the fuck am I doing using magic for this petty of a thing?\u201d, and that\u2019s an hounest epiphany right there, and very on theme for Mage<br /> <br /> 2. You would in that moment, feel that you are doing something *more* human in that moment , for lying to save your own ass and acting with the power you have been awarded are both *very* human if you take them generally. It\u2019s realizing that being human and being vampire aren\u2019t inherently exclusive, and it\u2019s often the little things that make you realize this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}